      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im seeing this weird 500 error on our /api/v1/checkout endpoint sometimes. it happens randomly during peak traffic but i cant replicate it in staging. here is the log snippet from the last crash:\n\nError: Internal Server Error\nat RequestHandler (/app/src/middleware/auth.js:42:11)\nat processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:95:5)\nUnhandledPromiseRejectionWarning: Timeout error connecting to redis_cache_cluster at 10.0.2.15:6379\n{ status: 500, code: 'ECONNRESET', detail: 'connection lost' }\n\nany idea what would cause this to be intermittent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The timeout and `ECONNRESET` errors suggest your Redis cache cluster is struggling under high load, likely due to connection pool exhaustion or network latency spikes. Since it only occurs during peak traffic, your Redis client is probably hitting its max connection limit or timing out because the cluster can't handle concurrent requests.\n\nI recommend checking your Redis connection pool settings (e.g., `maxRetriesPerRequest` or `enableReadyCheck`) and adding retry logic with exponential backoff. You should also monitor Redis CPU/memory usage and consider scaling your cluster or using a connection pooler like `ioredis`.\n\nAdditionally, wrap your auth middleware's Redis calls in a try/catch to return a graceful 503 instead of a 500 when the cache is temporarily unavailable.",
